  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TCPf: Enhancing Climate Change Resilience at the Water, Energy, and Food Nexus in Arid Land Countries</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Under the Technical Cooperation Programme Facility (TCPf) framework, FAO offices in the target countries closely collaborate with government partners to support the formulation of a concept note for water-food and energy (NEXUS) projects tailored to the unique challenges faced by each country. This project aligns with the national plans and strategies of Bahrain, Oman, Yemen, Egypt, and Tunisia, empowering these countries to adapt effectively to the adverse impacts of climate change. The innovative systems envisioned by FAO respond directly to the specific needs of each country, aligning with national initiatives and contributing significantly to the attainment of Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs). Through this strategic partnership, FAO, and the government?s aim to establish resilient and adaptive frameworks that ensure sustainable development and effectively address the complex challenges posed by climate change in the context of the water-food-energy nexus.</narrative>
  </description>
